{"id": "EUVD-2026-81790", "enisaUuid": "f99a7cfa-7038-3e38-90ad-3aa9670ced6f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: haptic: don't write an uninitialized value to unhandled usages\n\nfill_effect_buf() initializes value only for the four haptic usages\nhandled by its switch, but writes it to field->value[] for every usage.\nAn unhandled usage can therefore receive either an uninitialized value\nor one left over from the previous usage. hid_output_report() then\nserializes that value into the effect's report buffer.\n\nSkip unhandled usages instead. This also matches switch_mode(), which\nonly updates fields it recognizes.\n\nFound with Clang's -Wconditional-uninitialized.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:07:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:59:33", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/324cc98b71f0d3dee7367ef3c669fd80747e71b6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2d92c250815cba6bffd64f0125fac7afe4fa6ce0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3efb7f6491526f5012f9ec94769e9ed832feeef8"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90197", "GHSA-m8pj-r7fv-796q"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "31014b41-4f34-38ad-9279-9ce98b7fee9e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "344ff358495706abc7aac1e0c59a5bb16b350307 <2d92c250815cba6bffd64f0125fac7afe4fa6ce0"}, {"id": "593e2aec-f943-3e8c-9320-d2d149e8ec8f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "344ff358495706abc7aac1e0c59a5bb16b350307 <324cc98b71f0d3dee7367ef3c669fd80747e71b6"}, {"id": "5e7aa878-bdd9-3903-bd09-d15f832d94b6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "75230fef-e6c0-3d8e-92de-dddbf1fa92c6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "75258664-8364-39a9-af7b-0863ced36d54", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "c20af2c7-d84d-3be2-904c-d9d0a618f8ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "df24caef-68f5-361e-a86c-7beadddea641", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "ebdacf52-522e-3fa3-b626-01ef774a63cd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "344ff358495706abc7aac1e0c59a5bb16b350307 <3efb7f6491526f5012f9ec94769e9ed832feeef8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d3727742-93df-3eed-827c-a81e465c4fac", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}